        <body>
            <div xml:id="d194-a1">

                <pb facs="0347" n="233" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg233"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Annex<anchor n="30" xml:id="d194-f1"
                    />]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Aide-Mémoire</hi></head>
                <p>The British Government has called for the 17-th of this month a conference of
                    financial experts to determine the definite modalities of the proposal of the
                    President of the United States of America, to which the Yugoslav Government is
                    not invited to send its representative. By the order of the Royal Government,
                    the Royal Yugoslav Legation has the honor to inform the Department of State that
                    the Yugoslav Government considers that, at this conference, only the rights and
                    interests of those powers will be discussed among which a definite agreement has
                    been reached on the proposal to postpone the payments. In any event, the
                    Yugoslav Government considers it necessary formally to repeat the reservations
                    which it has made, when the intention of the President of the United States of
                    America to make the aforementioned proposal was communicated to it, and to
                    declare that, for the Yugoslav Government, only those decisions will be binding
                    which it will have been previously offered an opportunity to discuss and to
                    which it will have given its consent.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-13">July 13, 1931</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
